From: port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:44:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] il2cpp: replace the Doorstop entrypoint with a native one

Doorstop injects libdoorstop through LD_PRELOAD and then patches the managed
Main. Android has neither: the launcher ships libmain.so/libfusion.so, which
control the dlopen order of the game's libraries directly and bootstrap CoreCLR
from inside the il2cpp_init hook.

AndroidEntrypoint.Start therefore becomes the single entrypoint. fusion
resolves it through the runtime's load_assembly_and_get_function_pointer and
calls it once the domain exists.

NativeInterop declares the libfusion.so surface the managed layer needs
(logging plus the inline hook engine), so the detour code talks to the same
native library that hosts it instead of loading a second one.
